  "details": "The car model I have made for this world uses a single box collider with the friction set to 0 to collide with / move along the track (no wheel colliders). This is the comparison between how it behaves in Unity / ClientSim vs VRChat. I am just trying to drive normally around the course in both videos, not even touching left/right on straights.\n\nI can overcome this by using a series of capsule colliders in place of the box collider but this is a little less than ideal.\n\nUnity:\n\nhttps://drive.google.com/file/d/1PikA8kMSeo3H7HnXl05tgmtiWi_jELux/view?usp=sharing\n\nVRC:\n\nhttps://drive.google.com/file/d/10Vql_mYerQssZNlAq1MN3-g8m-xZs0vz/view?usp=sharing",
